-day Treasury bills in March totaled $4.7 billion and were refunded in an equal amount. The maturity and offering on March 6 were for $1.1 billion each and the maturities and offerings in the three remaining weeks were for $1.2 billion each. The average rates of discount on the new offerings were 1.657 percent for March 6, 1.784 percent for March 13, 1.601 percent for March 20, and 1.593 percent for March 27.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [196, 768, 243, 784], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"Note:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [259, 768, 851, 888], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"Details of Treasury market financing operations are shown elsewhere in this issue of the \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\", in the tables on\\\"Offerings\\\" and \\\"Disposition\\\", respectively, of marketable issues of bonds, notes, and certificates of indebtedness, and in the table \\\"Offerings of Treasury Bills\\\".\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [6, 11, 115, 46], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"April 1952\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1050, 8, 1066, 33], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"1\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [313, 59, 759, 85], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"SUMMARY OF FEDERAL FISCAL OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [448, 110, 624, 133], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [5, 133, 1048, 1193], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Period</th><th colspan=\\\"3\\\">Budget receipts and expenditures</th><th>Net of trust account and other transactions</th><th>Clearing account</th><th>Net increase in public debt, or decrease (-)</th