amounts transferred currently are approximately equal to the amounts transferred to the estimated of old-age insurance tax receipts made by the Secretary of the Treasury and are adjusted in later transfers on the basis of wage and self-employment income records maintained by the Federal Security Administrator.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [560, 1237, 618, 1296], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"8/9\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [588, 1134, 1079, 1344], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"For purposes of this table, the amount credited each month to the trust fund is included under \\\"Employment taxes\\\" as estimated receipts for old-age insurance. Throughout the calendar year 1951, the balance of the combined amounts paid in by employers was shown as income tax withheld. Beginning January 1952, the tax on self-employment income is allowed for in the amounts credited to the trust fund. These amounts therefore can no longer be used to derive estimates of income tax withheld by employers, but they are used to derive the estimates of total income and profits taxes. Interest on refunds is included in Table 5 under \\\"Miscellaneous\\\". Current appropriations were temporarily suspended to complete adjustments (see footnote 7) as follows: October 10 through November 5, 1951, for adjustment of $150 million ($113 million in October and $37 million in November); January 2 through 4, 1952, for adjustment of $25 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [27, 10, 38, 25], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"4\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [895, 5, 1074, 35], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [361, 56, 723, 71], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"BUDGET RE