aily Treasury Statement basis are compiled from the latest daily reports from Government depositaries; they do not coincide with amounts reported by collectors because of the lag in deposits of collections and because certain taxes are paid directly into the depositaries. Schedule A. Individual income tax. The tax base for the accounts is as follows: 1/ Include excise profits taxes formerly shown separately as follows: 2/ Just mentioned through 1947 (thereafter these collections are included in miscellaneous taxes); 3/ (thereafter, excise profits tax for ending after June 30, 1946). Profits Tax Act of 1940 (Title II of the Second Revenue Act of 1940, which was repealed for years ending December 31, 1945), and Vinson Act as amended (33 U.S.C. 496).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [582, 1141, 1071, 1350], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"3/ Includes social security tax on self-employment income, imposed by the Social Security Act Amendments of 1950 (Public Law 734), approved August 28, 1950. The tax is levied and collected as part of the individual income tax beginning with the taxable year 1951.\\nb/ Beginning January 1951, withheld income tax and social security employment taxes on employers and employees are paid into the Treasury in combined amounts without separation as 13% type of tax, pursuant to this Social Security Act Amendments of 1950. The figures for prior periods have been combined accordingly in this table for purposes of comparison, but are shown separately in the March 1951 and preceding issues of the \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\".\\n2/ For estimated 1951 breakdown, see Table 2, footnote 5.\\n3/ Repealed for years ending after June 30, 1945. Beginning July 1950, included under \\\"Miscellaneous taxes\\\".\\nr Revised.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1044, 29, 1066, 49], \"page_id\": 53}], \"content\": \"45\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"ty