950 → use 1950 rates\n\n\n- Period ending Feb 28, 1951 → use 1951 rates\n- Period ending Feb 29, 1952 → use 1952 rates\n\nActually, let me think about it more simply. The question is asking for the exchange rate to use. I'll use the year the period ends in. Since the periods end in February, I'll use rates from 1950, 1951, and 1952 respectively. But the World Bank data only goes back to 1976, so I'll need to find historical rates from other sources.\n\nI'll try checking the BIS database or the Federal Reserve's historical records since that aligns with their recommendation.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_cb805a3111054e0089c5ac6b","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"curl -sL \"https://www.bis.org/statistics/tc01_m1218.pdf\" 2>/dev/null | head -50"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
